  "decision": {
    "result": "promote exact aligned FP8 M64 attention-output projection",
    "why": "The route is bitwise exact, passes resource and invalid-contract gates, reaches 1.49086x in the isolated screen, improves every affected full-model prompt by 1.015764x to 1.025063x, and closes the intended launch transition in Nsight. The unchanged P33 fallback remains inside its 0.5% gate and improves in a longer control.",
    "decode_policy": "The non-MTP Decode anchor remains frozen at 105.870500 ms/token and 9.445501816 token/s.",
    "next_priority": "Screen test-only exact FP8 M64 [M64,N10240,K5120] linear-attention QKV against two production M32 launches, while running a separate non-production FlashInfer SM87/aarch64 and GQA 24:4/D256 compatibility probe."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "The formal result is batch-one, max1, one checkpoint, one device, fixed clocks, and mirrored process medians; it is not a serving-throughput or concurrency claim.",
    "P33 does not execute the new exact-M64 route. Its short formal sample regresses 0.316502% but remains inside the frozen 0.5% fallback gate; the longer matched control improves.",
    "The 1.49086x micro result and 1.355000x Nsight target-kernel result are phase-local and cannot be multiplied directly into whole-Prefix throughput.",
    "The independent user-reported vLLM plus FlashInfer 2k-8k token/s result remains non-comparable until model, precision, prompt accounting, concurrency, and hardware are aligned.",
    "This promotion does not add FlashInfer, MTP, continuous batching, a server, double/triple buffering, or Prefill/Decode overlap."
  ]
}
